\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A Short Guide to Otters\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Otters are 
\f0\b semiaquatic
\f1\b0  mammals. There are 14 species, and most live near fresh water.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What they eat\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Fish make up most of their diet. They also eat frogs, crabs, and shellfish, which sea otters open with stones.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Where they live\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Otters live on every continent except Australia and Antarctica.\
